Questions:

1. Shouldn't throwing Mjollnir at a disenchanter lower the
enchantment? (or indeed, any thrown weapon).

2. Pudding farming allows unlimited gain in AC and HP, and the
puddings also sometimes leave items. This is terribly abuseful.

3. I noticed spellcasting monsters getting stuck while above water on
the Castle level, but couldn't tie it down to a particular cause. Is
this a known bug, or not a bug?

4. Infinite numbers of Kops can be generated in minetown, and there is
a guaranteed altar, giving infinite sacrifices for nonhuman/chaotic
characters.

5. The PYEC allows infinite monster creation (via bag of tricks) and
infinite food (via horn of plenty)

6. You only need 1 !oS and 1 !oGE to turn hundreds of !oH into !oFH.
This makes huge HP increases easy.

7. In an extinctionist game, there's no point wishing for anything,
since it'll turn up eventually.

8. A creature summoned by the Wizard was carrying a magic lamp. Since
the wizard can summon indefinitely, and come back himself
indefinitely, this means unlimited wishes are possible.

I might come back to this game at some point in the future and carry
on doing insane things, like hollowing out every level with a pickaxe,
but for now, I just can't be bothered.

